{"name":"Sand Dollar","hex":"#dccdbb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sand dollar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any echinoderm of the order Clypeasteroida, having a flat, disk-shaped body with the mouth in a mid-ventral position, and living in sand, on or near the surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sand_dollar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sand dollar","blocks":[{"text":"Sand dollars are species of flat, burrowing sea urchins belonging to the order Clypeasteroida."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Clypeaster_reticulatus.jpg/330px-Clypeaster_reticulatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand_dollar","wikidata":"Q1071960"},{"title":"Sand","blocks":[{"text":"Sand is a granular material composed of finely divided mineral particles. Sand has various compositions but is usually defined by its grain size. Sand grains are smaller than gravel and coarser than silt. Sand can also refer to a textural class of soil or soil type; i.e., a soil containing more than 85 percent sand-sized particles by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg/330px-Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand","wikidata":"Q34679"},{"title":"Dollar","blocks":[{"text":"Dollar is the name of more than 25 currencies and their base units. The United States dollar, named after the international currency known as the Spanish dollar, was established in 1792 and is the first so named that still survives. Others include the Australian dollar, Brunei dollar, Canadian dollar, Eastern Caribbean dollar, Hong Kong dollar, Jamaican dollar, Liberian dollar, Namibian dollar, New Taiwan dollar, New Zealand dollar, Singapore dollar, Trinidad and Tobago dollar, and several others. The symbol for most of those currencies is the dollar sign $; the same symbol is used by many countries using peso currencies."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/Joachimsthaler_1525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dollar","wikidata":"Q14083"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)","wikidata":"Q9303163"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Leodia_sexiesperforata_derivada_2013.jpg/500px-Leodia_sexiesperforata_derivada_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Leodia_sexiesperforata_derivada_2013.jpg/500px-Leodia_sexiesperforata_derivada_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Leodia sexiesperforata by Louis Agassiz (1841)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeodia_sexiesperforata_derivada_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Rotulidae.JPG/500px-Rotulidae.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Rotulidae.JPG/500px-Rotulidae.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Examples of Rotulidae","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARotulidae.